<html>
<title>ROM, RAM, NVR, RTC</title>
<body>


<h1>ROM, RAM, NVR, RTC</h1>

<p>
Most computer configurations include one or two <strong>ROM @xxxx</strong>, <strong>RAM @xxxx</strong>, or <strong>NVR @xxxx</strong> buttons as shown in the screenshot below.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_rom_ram_nvr.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>ROM @xxxx</strong>, <strong>RAM @xxxx</strong> or <strong>NVR @xxxx</strong> buttons</li>
</ul>

<p>
These buttons load specific software into ROM, RAM, or NVR (non-volatile RAM) when the emulated computer starts. The XML file defines both the hexadecimal start address (@xxxx) and the default file location for each button.
</p>

<p>
To change the file location or filename, use the <strong>Browse</strong> button or type a new filename directly in the text field.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Note:</strong> ROM files in binary format (extensions <tt>.bin</tt>, <tt>.ch8</tt>, <tt>.c8x</tt>, <tt>.ch10</tt>, <tt>.sc8</tt>, <tt>.st2</tt>) will be loaded at the specified start address. Intel HEX files (extension <tt>.hex</tt>) and RCS Elf emulator HEX format files (extension <tt>.txt</tt>) include storage locations and will be loaded at the specified address locations.
</p>

<p>
During runtime, additional files can be loaded. See the <a href="ComputerMemAccess.htm">Memory Access</a>, <a href="ComputerDisk.htm">Disk Support</a>, <a href="ComputerCassette.htm">Cassette Support</a>, and <a href="ComputerModem.htm">HEX or XMODEM Support</a> sections.
</p>


<h2>NVR</h2>

<p>
To clear NVR memory at start-up, select the <strong>Clear non-volatile RAM</strong> checkbox. After start-up the emulator will automatically unselect the checkbox.
</p>


<h2>RTC</h2>

<p>
To clear RTC memory at start-up, select the <strong>Clear non-volatile RTC</strong> checkbox. After start-up the emulator will automatically unselect the checkbox.
</p>

</body>
</html>
